&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Konrad is a next-generation digital consultancy. We are dedicated to solving complex business problems for our global clients with creative and forward-thinking solutions. Our employees enjoy a culture built on innovation and a commitment to creating best-in-class digital products in use by hundreds of millions of consumers around the world. We hire exceptionally smart, analytical, and hard-working people who are lifelong learners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is part of our Digital team, where your internal title would be Associate, Digital; working primarily in a product analysis capacity across client engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Analyst, you are an early-to-mid career professional with a strong foundation in data-driven decision making and a desire to grow both your product and consulting skill set. Leveraging your analytical background, you will support the end-to-end lifecycle of digital products for our clients by tracking user behavior, evaluating product performance, and translating business objectives into technical requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with senior analysts, consultants, engineers, designers, and business stakeholders across a variety of client engagements, translating product visions and roadmaps into tangible digital products. With guidance and mentorship, you will support the delivery team with requirements documentation and process mapping while also building broader consulting skills across project management, user experience and product strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are curious, detail-oriented, and motivated to continuously improve your analytical and product capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support client and internal teams in defining key performance indicators (KPIs) and tracking success metrics for digital products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze user behaviour, conversion funnels, and feature usage to identify drop-off points, bottlenecks, and growth opportunities under the guidance of senior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and designers to formulate hypotheses, design experiments, and evaluate A/B test results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in creating documentation and visual artifacts, including telemetry specifications, data dictionaries, performance dashboards, and analytical reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering and data teams to ensure proper tracking implementation, data accuracy, and analytics governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate insights clearly through data visualizations, executive summaries, and presentation decks to inform roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify opportunities to improve product tracking methodologies, reporting efficiency, and client analytical frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in a product, data analyst, or digital strategy-focused role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management and collaboration tools (e.g. Jira, Confluence, Asana)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with data visualization platforms (e.g., Tableau, Power BI, Looker) and foundational knowledge of querying languages (e.g., SQL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of digital product lifecycles, product management frameworks, and Agile/Scrum environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience synthesizing complex data sets into clear, actionable insights for diverse stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and quantitative problem-solving skills with high attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in cross-functional and consulting-style environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in learning about emerging digital trends, user behavioural patterns, and product-led growth strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Health &amp;amp; Wellness Benefits Package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Working Hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home Flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service Recognition Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Socials, Outings &amp;amp; Retreats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture of Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt; Have you taken any courses at BrainStation? A lot of our design and development best practices and processes are taught during our courses, make sure to highlight this experience in your cover letter if you have!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Konrad is committed to maintaining a diverse work environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants, regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status will receive consideration for employment. If you have any accessibility requirements or concerns regarding the hiring process or employment with us, please notify us so we can provide suitable accommodation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated compensation for this position is $78,000 - $90,000. This is an estimate and a compensation offer will vary based on applicant’s education, experience, skills, abilities and alignment with market data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we sincerely appreciate all applications, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
